        "semantics": "DexJoCo's own action row. The arm tracks the tcp target through DexJoCo's operational-space controller (it lags a moving target and stops where contact blocks it); the hand joints are position-controlled. Rows are `dt` apart (a whole multiple of 1/50 s, at most 0.5 s); between rows positions and joints move linearly and orientations by slerp (`linear`) or jump (`hold`); a row's own values land exactly on its last control step. Hand targets outside the ranges are clamped by the simulator and reported in `clipped`; a zero quaternion is a 400."
